    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for looking into it. i was thinking about what you said about a \"previously unknown phenomenon.\" \n\nif this isn't just solar pressure or glitches, the timing is what's really messing with me. it's not random, but it's not a standard broadcast either. if you look at the intervals between the signal dips, they don't match any known satellite handoff protocol. \n\ncould these \"dips\" actually be a way of encoding data? like, if someone wanted to pass a message through a high-traffic network without actually being \"on\" the frequency, they could just manipulate the signal strength in a specific sequence. does that kind of pattern-based signaling ring any bells to you? it feels like it's hiding in plain sight.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
